## Lifecycle and Ownership

Only superusers and `sys:secadmin` holders can change these settings. While RLS is on, a user sees only the rows that an
attached policy permits and no rows at all when no policy applies to them, so attach the policies before turning RLS on.
`conjunction_type` and `datashare_row_level_security` change in place; when unset, the resource keeps and reports what
the relation already has. `ROW LEVEL SECURITY OFF FOR DATASHARES` makes the relation readable over datashares without
row filtering on the consumer side, while the producer keeps RLS.

The resource never creates or drops the relation and never reads its columns, policies, or attachments. Reads use
`svv_rls_relation`; a relation that view does not list has never been protected and reports RLS off, `AND`, and RLS on
for datashares. A dropped relation or database removes the resource from state. Deletion only turns RLS off; the
conjunction type and datashare setting stay as they are.

